# CVE Exception List for pip-audit (SPEC-082, RF-05)
# ===================================================
# Format: CVE-ID | Package | Reason | Decision Date | Review Date
#
# POLICY (SPEC-082, RFC-05):
# - Exceptions are NEVER automatic or global ("ignore all HIGH/CRITICAL")
# - Each exception requires: CVE ID, package name, justification, and decision date
# - Decision to add an exception is made by the LEAD, never the agent
# - Exceptions are auditable and tracked in version control
# - Each exception must include a review date (when it should be re-evaluated)
# - NO CONFIDENTIAL DATA in this file (only CVE IDs, package names, and generic reasons)
#
# HOW TO ADD AN EXCEPTION (requires LEAD approval):
#   1. Identify the CVE ID (e.g., PYSEC-2024-48 for black 23.12.1)
#   2. Verify it's in the pip-audit report: `pip-audit --desc --skip-editable`
#   3. Document package name, business justification, decision date, and review date
#   4. Uncomment/add the line below (following format exactly)
#   5. The CI workflow will parse this file and pass --ignore-vuln flags to pip-audit
#   6. Create a commit with message: "chore(security): exception CVE-XXXX (reason, review YYYY-MM-DD)"
#
# CURRENT EXCEPTIONS:
# (none — list is empty by design; any future exception requires LEAD approval)
#
# EXAMPLES (DO NOT UNCOMMENT — for reference only):
